      "reason": "the sheet publishes both, and both are right: it measures its Vicat point at 5 kg (\"ASTM D1525 5kg, 50°C/h\", \"ISO 306 5kg\"), which is the heavy load, and a needle under 50 N goes into a bar as soon as the polymer softens. A Vicat at or just below the glass transition is what that load gives; the rule is drawn from sheets that state the light one. It is systematic across this maker’s library.",
